---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import DefaultLayout from '../layouts/DefaultLayout.astro'
import Section from '../components/Section.astro'
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro'
import KeepExploring from '../components/KeepExploring.astro'
import travelPhoto from '../assets/photos/cruise-terminal.jpg'
import tippingPhoto from '../assets/photos/enchanted-garden.jpg'
import kidsPhoto from '../assets/photos/oceaneer-club.jpg'
import packingPhoto from '../assets/photos/castaway-cay.jpg'
---

<DefaultLayout title="Plan">
  <PageHero lede="Travel, lodging, packing, and what to expect onboard.">
    Plan your trip
  </PageHero>

  <Section class="plan-highlights" rule={false}>
    <header class="highlights-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Before you sail</span>
      <p class="highlights-lede">The handful of things worth sorting out early. Jump to any point for the details.</p>
    </header>
    <ul class="highlights-list">
      <li>
        <a href="#getting-there">
          <span class="hl-title">Book flights now — and fly in the night before</span>
          <span class="hl-note">A delayed morning flight means a missed ship. It sails on schedule and will not wait.</span>
          <span class="hl-jump">Travel &amp; lodging</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#boarding-bag">
          <span class="hl-title">Pack a boarding-day bag</span>
          <span class="hl-note">Checked luggage reaches your stateroom hours after boarding — carry a swimsuit, medication, and wallet with you.</span>
          <span class="hl-jump">Packing</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#themed-nights">
          <span class="hl-title">Night 4 is Pirate Night</span>
          <span class="hl-note">A pool-deck party with a stage show, characters, and fireworks. Pack a costume if you'd like to dress up.</span>
          <span class="hl-jump">Packing</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#group">
          <span class="hl-title">We're together at dinner every night</span>
          <span class="hl-note">If you haven't already, send Jackie your reservation number so the whole group is seated together.</span>
          <span class="hl-jump">Group plans</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/itinerary#day-4">
          <span class="hl-title">Group lunch in Nassau, Day 4</span>
          <span class="hl-note">Noon–4 PM ashore. The ship docks at 8 AM and all guests must be back aboard by 5:30 PM.</span>
          <span class="hl-jump">Itinerary</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#staying-connected">
          <span class="hl-title">Get the Disney Cruise Line app</span>
          <span class="hl-note">Daily schedule, deck maps, and free onboard texting over WiFi. Leave the walkie-talkies at home.</span>
          <span class="hl-jump">Onboard essentials</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#drinks-onboard">
          <span class="hl-title">Know what's free to drink</span>
          <span class="hl-note">Sodas and drip coffee are included; there's no drink package. Guests 21+ may bring a limited amount of wine or beer aboard.</span>
          <span class="hl-jump">Onboard essentials</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section id="group" class="plan-group">
    <header class="block-head group-head">
      <h2 class="block-title">Group plans</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="plan-group-note">
      <p>
        Our whole group has tables booked together for dinner every night in the rotational dining rooms — if you haven't already, send Jackie your reservation number so we can seat everyone together. Beyond that there are no planned events before or after the cruise. The one daytime gathering is a <strong>group lunch in Nassau on Day 4, noon–4 PM</strong>. Transportation is still being sorted (the current plan is individual taxis, though we're looking into chartered transport). The ship docks at 8 AM, so there's time to explore Nassau or the ship beforehand — just leave yourself buffer to be back aboard well before the 5:30 PM all-aboard, especially if it's your first cruise.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section id="travel" class="plan-block">
    <div class="plan-aside">
      <figure class="plan-photo">
        <Image src={travelPhoto} alt="Disney Cruise Line Terminal at Port Canaveral" />
      </figure>
      <div class="plan-aside-body">
        <header class="block-head">
          <span class="block-num">01</span>
          <h2 class="block-title">Travel & lodging</h2>
        </header>
        <h3 class="block-sub">Online check-in</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Online check-in opens 30 days before sailing through the Disney Cruise Line app. Complete it as early as possible to lock in an earlier port-arrival window. Register everyone in your party, including kids, so they're ready to join the kids' clubs the moment you're onboard. Waiting until the ship means standing in the in-person registration line on embarkation day.
        </p>
        <h3 id="getting-there" class="block-sub">Getting there</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Book flights as early as you can, and fly in the night before. The ship departs on schedule — if a same-day flight is delayed the morning of embarkation, it will not wait, and a missed departure is on you. The drive from Orlando International (MCO) to Port Canaveral is about an hour, so the night before leaves comfortable buffer.
        </p>
        <h3 class="block-sub">Where to stay</h3>
        <ul class="block-list">
          <li><strong>Hyatt Regency Orlando Airport (MCO).</strong> Inside the terminal — book the Disney Cruise transfer add-on (about $45 per person, one-way) for direct transport to the port plus the chance of an earlier boarding window.</li>
          <li><strong>Disney resort area or Disney Springs.</strong> Best if you want to spend a day at Disney Springs or the parks before the cruise. Paid shuttles from Disney resorts to the port can also be arranged by calling the hotel ahead of time.</li>
          <li><strong>Port Canaveral / Cocoa Beach.</strong> Closest to the ship — five to fifteen minutes by car. Best if you're arriving morning-of or just the night before with no Disney plans.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 class="block-sub">Getting to the ship</h3>
        <p class="block-body">Disney's Cruise transfer is the easiest path from MCO or a Disney hotel. Driving yourself is fine — Port Canaveral has paid parking on-site ($20 per day). Rideshare runs to the port too.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section id="onboard" class="plan-block">
    <div class="plan-aside">
      <figure class="plan-photo">
        <Image src={tippingPhoto} alt="Enchanted Garden dining room aboard the Disney Fantasy" />
      </figure>
      <div class="plan-aside-body">
        <header class="block-head">
          <span class="block-num">02</span>
          <h2 class="block-title">Onboard essentials</h2>
        </header>
        <h3 class="block-sub">Gratuities</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Disney auto-adds standard gratuities (server, assistant server, head server, stateroom host) to your onboard account at <strong>$16.00 per guest per night</strong>. You can adjust amounts at Guest Services.
        </p>
        <h3 class="block-sub">Cash</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Bring cash for port vendors, taxis ashore, optional gratuities (spa, kids' clubs, port-adventure guides), and incidentals. Onboard is otherwise cashless — your stateroom key is your charge card.
        </p>
        <h3 id="drinks-onboard" class="block-sub">Drinks onboard</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Disney doesn't sell an all-inclusive drinks package; you pay per drink. Soft drinks are complimentary at meals and at the 24-hour pool-deck beverage stations, as is standard drip coffee in the main dining rooms, buffet, quick-service spots, and room service. Sodas at the bars, bottled water, beer, wine, cocktails, smoothies, and specialty espresso (lattes, cold brew, iced coffee) all carry a charge.
        </p>
        <p class="block-body">
          Each bar runs a cocktail and mocktail of the day at lower-than-menu prices. Vibe (the teen lounge) serves complimentary soft drinks, with a charge for smoothies.
        </p>
        <h3 class="block-sub">Room service</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Available 24 hours and included — order to the stateroom anytime at no charge. A tip for the delivery crew member is expected, so keep small bills on hand.
        </p>
        <h3 id="staying-connected" class="block-sub">Staying connected</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Everyone should install the <a class="block-link" href="https://disneycruise.disney.go.com/featured/navigator-app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Disney Cruise Line app</strong></a> before sailing — it carries the daily schedule, ship maps, hours, and character times. WiFi isn't included in the fare, but once connected you can send texts, iMessages, and WhatsApp messages for free (no photos or video). The app also has a free onboard chat, though it can be unreliable. Leave walkie-talkies at home — they aren't permitted and don't work well through the ship's metal walls anyway.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section class="plan-block">
    <div class="plan-aside">
      <figure class="plan-photo">
        <Image src={kidsPhoto} alt="Disney's Oceaneer Club kids space" />
      </figure>
      <div class="plan-aside-body">
        <header class="block-head">
          <span class="block-num">03</span>
          <h2 class="block-title">Kids clubs</h2>
        </header>
        <p class="block-body">
          Programs are split by age. The Nursery is the only space that takes (and requires) reservations; every other club is walk-in — no other reservations are accepted. Open houses run on embarkation day and throughout the cruise so parents can tour the spaces.
        </p>

        <h3 class="block-sub">The spaces</h3>
        <ul class="block-list">
          <li><strong>It's a Small World Nursery</strong> — 6 months to 3 years. Paid, hourly rate. Reserve in the app as soon as your booking window opens.</li>
          <li><strong>Disney's Oceaneer Club & Lab</strong> — 3 to 10 years. Included. Themed play areas for Toy Story, Star Wars, Marvel, and Tinker Bell, plus Disney-led activities throughout the day.</li>
          <li><strong>Edge</strong> — 11 to 14 years. Included. Tween-only hangout.</li>
          <li><strong>Vibe</strong> — 14 to 17 years. Included. Teen-only space with its own pool deck, beverage bar, and loungers.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="block-body">
          For a walk-through of all four spaces on the Fantasy, see <a class="block-link" href="https://youtu.be/ha7miJb7GWQ?si=N6rNzlU_snokkuSP" target="_blank" rel="noopener">this overview video</a>.
        </p>

        <h3 class="block-sub">Drop-off & pickup</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Kids receive a Disney Oceaneer Band at boarding — staff use it to check them in and out. Return it before disembarkation or your account will be charged for it. An existing MagicBand+ or DisneyBand+ (or one you buy ahead of the cruise) works as a substitute.
        </p>
        <p class="block-body">
          At check-in you'll choose a codeword used every time someone picks the kids up. Pick something the whole family will remember.
        </p>

        <h3 class="block-sub">Schedules, meals & ashore</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Hours shift day to day — check the Disney Cruise Line app for the live schedule. It also lists character meet-and-greets (Doctor Strange, etc.) and special club activities. Meals are not included in club hours; plan to pick kids up for dinner. Kids' programming also runs at the private islands.
        </p>

        <h3 class="block-sub">Beyond the clubs</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          <strong>The Midship Detective Agency</strong> — an interactive whodunit that turns the ship into a board game. Pick up case files at the activity desk, then use the Enchanted Art panels scattered across the decks (the artwork comes to life when you scan your detective badge) to gather clues and solve the mystery.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section id="packing" class="plan-block" rule={false}>
    <div class="plan-aside">
      <figure class="plan-photo">
        <Image src={packingPhoto} alt="Castaway Cay beach" />
      </figure>
      <div class="plan-aside-body">
        <header class="block-head">
          <span class="block-num">04</span>
          <h2 class="block-title">Packing</h2>
        </header>

        <h3 id="boarding-bag" class="block-sub">Your boarding-day bag</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          At the port, porters take your checked luggage and deliver it to your stateroom — but that can take a few hours. Pack a carry-on with anything you'll want right away: a swimsuit for the pool, medication, your wallet, phone chargers, and travel documents. That way you're set to enjoy the ship the moment you're aboard.
        </p>

        <h3 class="block-sub">Weather (late August Bahamas)</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          Hot and humid. Daytime highs near 88°F, evenings around 75°F. Pack rain gear — afternoon thunderstorms are common. Strong sun: bring reef-safe sunscreen for the islands.
        </p>

        <h3 id="themed-nights" class="block-sub">Themed nights onboard</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          <strong>Night 2 — Semi-formal (optional).</strong> Bring a dressy outfit if you'd like to participate.<br>
          <strong>Night 4 — Pirate Night.</strong> A big one on Disney cruises: a pool-deck party with a stage show, characters, and fireworks at sea. Dress-up is optional, but plenty of guests go for it. Disney sells gear onboard but it's pricey; packing a costume is easier.
        </p>

        <h3 class="block-sub">Alcohol policy</h3>
        <ul class="block-list">
          <li><strong>Carry-on only, 21+.</strong> One unopened 750ml bottle of wine or sparkling wine, or six 12oz beers per guest, packed in carry-on at initial embarkation. Alcohol in checked luggage is removed and not returned.</li>
          <li><strong>Sealed bottles only.</strong> Broken seals or anything beyond the allowance is discarded at the gangway with no compensation.</li>
          <li><strong>Where you can drink it.</strong> Carry-on bottles stay in the stateroom; lounges and public areas are off-limits for outside alcohol. A $20 per-bottle corkage fee applies if you bring wine to a dining room.</li>
          <li><strong>Port purchases.</strong> Alcohol bought ashore is collected at the gangway and returned at the end of the cruise. Unclaimed bottles are discarded.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="block-sub">Prohibited items</h3>
        <p class="block-body">
          No irons, candles, halogen lamps, hot plates, drones, illegal substances, or surge protectors with cords. Disney provides an iron at Guest Services if you need to press something.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <KeepExploring current="plan" />
</DefaultLayout>

<style lang="scss">
  // ── Before-you-sail highlights ──────────────────────────
  .highlights-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .highlights-head .eyebrow {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .highlights-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-family-body);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .highlights-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .highlights-list li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .highlights-list a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    grid-template-areas:
      'title jump'
      'note jump';
    align-items: baseline;
    column-gap: var(--space-md);
    row-gap: 4px;
    padding: var(--space-md) 4px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .hl-title {
    grid-area: title;
    font-family: var(--font-family-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--ink);
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .hl-note {
    grid-area: note;
    font-family: var(--font-family-body);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .hl-jump {
    grid-area: jump;
    align-self: center;
    font-family: var(--font-family-label);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .hl-jump::after {
    content: ' →';
  }

  .highlights-list a:hover .hl-title,
  .highlights-list a:focus-visible .hl-title,
  .highlights-list a:hover .hl-jump,
  .highlights-list a:focus-visible .hl-jump {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .highlights-list a {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      grid-template-areas:
        'title'
        'note'
        'jump';
      row-gap: 6px;
    }
    .hl-jump {
      align-self: start;
    }
  }

  // ── group note ──────────────────────────────────────────
  .plan-group-note p {
    font-family: var(--font-family-body);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .plan-group-note p strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  // anchored sections clear the top edge when jumped to
  .plan-highlights,
  .plan-group,
  .plan-block,
  .block-sub {
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .plan-photo {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg);
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .plan-photo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .plan-aside {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, 1fr) 1.6fr;
    gap: 29px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .plan-aside .plan-photo {
    margin: 0;
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
  }

  .plan-aside-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .plan-aside-body .block-head {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .plan-aside {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 19px;
    }
    .plan-aside .plan-photo {
      aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    }
  }

  .block-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .block-num {
    font-family: var(--font-family-label);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 2.5px;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
  }

  .block-title {
    font-family: var(--font-family-display);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 40px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .block-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-family-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-xs);
  }

  .block-body {
    font-family: var(--font-family-body);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }

  .block-body strong { font-weight: 600; }

  .block-link {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--gold);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }

  .block-link:hover {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  .block-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .block-list li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: var(--space-md) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-family-body);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .block-list li strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
</style>
